<description>&lt;p&gt;Egypt reopened its embassy in Tripoli, restoring diplomatic ties after a 12 year gap. ISIS militants killed a young Christian man in Libya after he refused to deny Jesus. A fire triggered an explosion at a gas complex in Marsa Brega, killing one worker and injuring four, while authorities detained a translator and arrested a man in Tripoli for throwing grenades at the army. Libya and Chad signed the final document of the CEN SAD Executive Council meeting and combat intensity remains low, with 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxOUmxJSTBtNC0zNWtPUkRhQ1JxS2dCRndtN3o1cURid3ZkdTRjTmthSmRubHJONFNBYlFLT1MwVGVyUENyNnYyYTU3Rnp5YjRSa3Z0NWprOWl6ckx4T3hXS3dGeThhZjlzWHFZSDNrX2VabUlaZWhKQUJORlJBYlFqNTJNYWRCaWcxLWhDTkxIRVl2Q2JvYlFVajdlN050dlI0?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxNU0Y3N3dwVkdGV1BpRmwxQ0FIYmYxVlRabkE2VU96bEVLMVhGVG01VTd6VDdpWFM0bktUSTZJczFsX2pHWWZ6SjN3RUVBbGRwaGJJUWtOUUFWcW1CUVV6bzItdjNHVm0zUmJ5VEI4RVhDLUV2RFV4Z3d5NGphSER3cXFBTHg3RDV3Smg4c0tUTVFTUHg0X2paSmRORWk?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiV0FVX3lxTE9DU1A1RDZfTHZpSkthYlNpN0dUb2FjSzR1THV5Tk80R3h6Qy1DNmg0WW90QmZHWnpCNk1KTkZMd1pjRkRmRzdZR2x5VFRtTG9YejVYRHBpRQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxPOXI1N0JOdFRfNV9BZDFZMmxJM2tDTUo2alppRGlPU1hUckJjR0prNkEwN3NyVVpiWE1nSnctQ3dEaHdoZkdRNzh5QlhKRko0NVRfOXdFT21oWVBEbUUybHUyQzV2UXZrQmFWOU1xMEwwbnFxdXR6STlSSThaaGVYU0V1bWRSSFRfNGdISGMzUGwxeE9wYmFmVVhIX2x3LThCOGp0TllmVUFETnlfcVBFMDNfeXhPMTlNN09PU0xLTl9GQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sahara Reporters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxQY2hCTHExVDF1M1Q3OVVLcUFOQ1FZR